 # Docker Lifecycle Learning App

 This is a small learning and testing application for understanding the Docker container lifecycle.

 ## Learning goals

 - Build an image from a Dockerfile
 - Create and run containers
 - Inspect container status and logs
 - Start, stop, restart, and remove containers
 - Understand the difference between images, containers, and volumes

 ## Prerequisites

 - [Docker](https://docs.docker.com/get-docker/) installed and running
 - A terminal or command prompt

 ## Getting started

 Clone or open this project, then build the image:

 ```bash
 docker build -t docker-lifecycle-app .
 ```

 Run a container:

 ```bash
 docker run --name docker-lifecycle-container docker-lifecycle-app
 ```

 ## Useful lifecycle commands

 ```bash
 # List running containers
 docker ps

 # List all containers
 docker ps -a

 # View container output
 docker logs docker-lifecycle-container

 # Stop and start a container
 docker stop docker-lifecycle-container
 docker start docker-lifecycle-container

 # Restart a container
 docker restart docker-lifecycle-container

 # Remove a stopped container
 docker rm docker-lifecycle-container

 # Remove the image
 docker rmi docker-lifecycle-app
 ```

 ## Lifecycle overview

 ```text
 Dockerfile -> Image -> Created container -> Running -> Stopped -> Removed
 ```

 Use the commands above to observe each state and experiment safely.
